<%# Upstream's "Size" and "Disabled".

    Icon-only items, because that is where the size shows. The three are
    `h-8 min-w-8`, `h-9 min-w-9` and `h-10 min-w-10` — with a text label the
    width comes from the text and only 4px of height separates them, which is
    what the first version of this preview looked like: three rows the same.

    Upstream's "Vertical" is not here. `toggle-group.tsx` takes no orientation
    at all, so there is nothing in this registry to show — the first version
    passed `orientation:`, which landed as an inert HTML attribute, and the
    version after it reached for `flex-col`, which stacks items of three
    different widths because the group is `w-fit`. Both were this port
    inventing a variant. See todo.md for the others upstream's docs show and
    this registry does not have. %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-6">
  <% %i[sm default lg].each do |size| %>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
      <%= render(Shadcn::ToggleGroup::Component.new(type: :single, variant: :outline, size:, value: "check")) do |g| %>
        <% %w[check circle x].each do |icon| %>
          <% g.with_item(value: icon, pressed: icon == "check", "aria-label": icon) do %>
            <%= render(Shadcn::Icon::Component.new(icon)) %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= size %></span>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
    <%= render(Shadcn::ToggleGroup::Component.new(type: :single, variant: :outline, disabled: true, value: "b")) do |g| %>
      <% %w[A B C].each do |label| %>
        <% g.with_item(value: label.downcase, pressed: label == "B") { label } %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">disabled</span>
  </div>
</div>
